1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,831
Carry a bag up the
stairs, or up a long ramp.

2
00:00:03,831 --> 00:00:06,776
Ride up a steep road, or a winding one.

3
00:00:07,176 --> 00:00:08,839
You end at the same height.

4
00:00:08,839 --> 00:00:11,156
So does gravity care which way you went?

5
00:00:11,606 --> 00:00:13,819
Aarav wants to ride to the hilltop.

6
00:00:13,819 --> 00:00:17,485
A steep path climbs sixty metres
in just three hundred metres.

7
00:00:17,834 --> 00:00:21,842
The winding road reaches the same top,
but it is one point two kilometres

8
00:00:21,842 --> 00:00:22,742
long.

9
00:00:22,326 --> 00:00:24,900
Where does gravity take
more energy from him?

10
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:27,001
By the end, you will know.

11
00:00:27,001 --> 00:00:29,295
And you will see why
friction is different.

12
00:00:29,945 --> 00:00:32,135
So what is a conservative force?

13
00:00:32,485 --> 00:00:34,358
Gravity only checks two things.

14
00:00:34,358 --> 00:00:36,606
Where you start, and where you end.

15
00:00:37,006 --> 00:00:39,833
The path in between does
not change its work.

16
00:00:39,833 --> 00:00:42,363
A force like this is called conservative.

17
00:00:42,763 --> 00:00:44,187
Friction is different.

18
00:00:44,187 --> 00:00:47,298
Every metre you slide, it
takes away more energy.

19
00:00:47,698 --> 00:00:49,315
Its work depends on the path.

20
00:00:49,315 --> 00:00:51,568
A force like this is
called non-conservative.

21
00:00:52,218 --> 00:00:53,238
Let's test it.

22
00:00:53,238 --> 00:00:57,525
A three kilogram box goes from the
floor to a shelf, two metres up.

23
00:00:57,875 --> 00:00:58,775
Path one.

24
00:00:58,625 --> 00:01:00,308
Straight up, then across.

25
00:01:00,308 --> 00:01:03,737
Gravity does minus fifty eight
point eight joules of work.

26
00:01:04,137 --> 00:01:05,037
Path two.

27
00:01:04,914 --> 00:01:07,406
Push it up a ramp, four metres long.

28
00:01:07,806 --> 00:01:10,865
Gravity's work is again minus
fifty eight point eight joules.

29
00:01:11,265 --> 00:01:13,105
Path three, a staircase.

30
00:01:13,105 --> 00:01:14,472
Same answer again.

31
00:01:14,472 --> 00:01:16,630
Three paths, one finish line.

32
00:01:17,030 --> 00:01:19,016
Now slide it back down the ramp.

33
00:01:19,016 --> 00:01:21,484
Gravity gives back
fifty eight point eight.

34
00:01:21,884 --> 00:01:23,489
Round trip total: zero.

35
00:01:24,089 --> 00:01:26,177
Slow-mo replay, on the ramp.

36
00:01:26,527 --> 00:01:28,279
Gravity points straight down.

37
00:01:28,279 --> 00:01:31,170
Only the up and down part
of the motion counts.

38
00:01:31,170 --> 00:01:32,606
Sideways gets no work.

39
00:01:33,256 --> 00:01:35,246
Now the reason, step by step.

40
00:01:35,596 --> 00:01:36,496
Step one.

41
00:01:36,378 --> 00:01:38,437
Break any path into tiny steps.

42
00:01:38,437 --> 00:01:41,393
Each step has a sideways
part and an up part.

43
00:01:42,143 --> 00:01:43,043
Step two.

44
00:01:42,893 --> 00:01:46,135
Sideways, gravity is at
ninety degrees to the motion.

45
00:01:46,135 --> 00:01:47,554
So its work is zero.

46
00:01:48,304 --> 00:01:49,258
Step three.

47
00:01:49,258 --> 00:01:54,132
Going up by a tiny height, delta
y, gravity does minus m g delta y.

48
00:01:54,882 --> 00:01:55,782
Step four.

49
00:01:55,777 --> 00:01:57,206
Add all the steps.

50
00:01:57,206 --> 00:02:00,724
The work is minus m g,
times y two minus y one.

51
00:02:01,474 --> 00:02:02,374
Step five.

52
00:02:02,306 --> 00:02:05,519
Come back to the start,
and y two equals y one.

53
00:02:05,519 --> 00:02:07,441
The round trip work is zero.

54
00:02:08,191 --> 00:02:09,243
Remember this.

55
00:02:09,243 --> 00:02:13,704
A conservative force does the same
work on every path, and zero work on

56
00:02:13,704 --> 00:02:14,765
a round trip.

57
00:02:15,465 --> 00:02:16,365
Now friction.

58
00:02:16,328 --> 00:02:17,410
Follow the links.

59
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:18,660
One.

60
00:02:18,233 --> 00:02:20,745
Friction always points against the motion.

61
00:02:21,145 --> 00:02:22,045
Two.

62
00:02:21,625 --> 00:02:24,930
So on every bit of the
path, its work is negative.

63
00:02:25,330 --> 00:02:26,230
Three.

64
00:02:25,903 --> 00:02:27,631
Negative bits never cancel.

65
00:02:27,631 --> 00:02:30,628
The longer the path, the
more energy it takes.

66
00:02:31,028 --> 00:02:31,928
Four.

67
00:02:31,561 --> 00:02:33,924
So the round trip work is not zero.

68
00:02:33,924 --> 00:02:35,734
The energy turns into heat.

69
00:02:36,334 --> 00:02:37,756
Now, side by side.

70
00:02:38,106 --> 00:02:41,926
Slide the box six metres,
against ten newtons of friction.

71
00:02:41,926 --> 00:02:43,295
Minus sixty joules.

72
00:02:43,695 --> 00:02:46,264
The long way round is twelve metres.

73
00:02:46,264 --> 00:02:48,770
Minus one hundred and twenty joules.

74
00:02:48,770 --> 00:02:49,945
Twice as much.

75
00:02:50,545 --> 00:02:51,512
Now you try.

76
00:02:51,512 --> 00:02:55,401
Carry a bag up to the third
floor and back down to the start.

77
00:02:55,401 --> 00:02:57,186
Total work done by gravity?

78
00:02:57,186 --> 00:02:58,388
Pause and decide.

79
00:03:01,588 --> 00:03:02,488
Zero!

80
00:03:02,099 --> 00:03:04,081
It is back at the same height.

81
00:03:04,081 --> 00:03:07,934
Gravity took energy going up,
and gave it all back coming down.

82
00:03:08,584 --> 00:03:09,484
One more.

83
00:03:09,316 --> 00:03:12,271
A ball is thrown up and
falls back to your hand.

84
00:03:12,271 --> 00:03:14,485
Is the total work by air drag zero?

85
00:03:14,485 --> 00:03:15,583
Pause and think.

86
00:03:18,783 --> 00:03:19,683
No!

87
00:03:19,218 --> 00:03:22,891
Drag points down on the way
up, and up on the way down.

88
00:03:22,891 --> 00:03:24,444
Both bits are negative.

89
00:03:25,094 --> 00:03:26,784
Now, one worked example.

90
00:03:27,134 --> 00:03:30,377
Aarav and his bicycle have
a mass of seventy kilograms.

91
00:03:30,377 --> 00:03:32,971
Air and road push back
with twenty newtons.

92
00:03:33,471 --> 00:03:34,605
Gravity first.

93
00:03:34,605 --> 00:03:37,593
Seventy times nine
point eight times sixty.

94
00:03:37,593 --> 00:03:42,381
Minus forty one thousand one hundred
and sixty joules, on both paths.

95
00:03:43,131 --> 00:03:45,511
Now the resistance on the steep path.

96
00:03:45,511 --> 00:03:48,070
Twenty newtons times three hundred metres.

97
00:03:48,070 --> 00:03:49,760
Minus six thousand joules.

98
00:03:50,510 --> 00:03:53,656
On the winding road, twenty
times twelve hundred.

99
00:03:53,656 --> 00:03:55,814
Minus twenty four thousand joules.

100
00:03:56,564 --> 00:03:58,988
Gravity does not care about the path.

101
00:03:58,988 --> 00:04:01,951
Resistance does, four
times more on the road.

102
00:04:02,601 --> 00:04:04,063
Now, the exam trap.

103
00:04:04,413 --> 00:04:08,024
Many students say a conservative
force always does zero work.

104
00:04:08,374 --> 00:04:10,949
But it is zero only on a closed path.

105
00:04:10,949 --> 00:04:15,104
Floor to shelf, gravity did minus
fifty eight point eight joules.

106
00:04:15,754 --> 00:04:17,037
Where is this asked?

107
00:04:17,037 --> 00:04:21,006
In one mark questions on conservative
forces, and round trip numericals.

108
00:04:21,606 --> 00:04:22,826
Exam level now.

109
00:04:22,826 --> 00:04:27,519
A two kilogram block is pulled up a
rough incline, five metres long and

110
00:04:27,519 --> 00:04:30,434
three metres high, then slides back down.

111
00:04:30,434 --> 00:04:32,946
mu is zero point five, g is ten.

112
00:04:32,946 --> 00:04:36,885
Total work by gravity and by
friction over the round trip?

113
00:04:36,885 --> 00:04:38,157
Pause and solve.

114
00:04:43,557 --> 00:04:44,867
The answer is A.

115
00:04:44,867 --> 00:04:47,050
Zero, and minus eighty joules.

116
00:04:47,550 --> 00:04:49,123
Gravity is conservative.

117
00:04:49,123 --> 00:04:52,655
The block ends where it
started, so its work is zero.

118
00:04:53,155 --> 00:04:56,728
The incline has sine three
fifths, so cos four fifths.

119
00:04:56,728 --> 00:05:00,095
Normal force: two times
ten times zero point eight.

120
00:05:00,095 --> 00:05:01,240
Sixteen newtons.

121
00:05:01,740 --> 00:05:04,251
Friction is zero point five times sixteen.

122
00:05:04,251 --> 00:05:06,943
Eight newtons, against
the motion both ways.

123
00:05:07,443 --> 00:05:10,773
Over ten metres, it does
minus eight times ten.

124
00:05:10,773 --> 00:05:12,243
Minus eighty joules.

125
00:05:12,843 --> 00:05:14,383
Here is your recap.

126
00:05:14,383 --> 00:05:15,966
Screenshot this card.

127
00:05:19,166 --> 00:05:21,352
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

128
00:05:21,752 --> 00:05:22,652
One.

129
00:05:22,115 --> 00:05:23,646
What makes a force conservative?

130
00:05:24,546 --> 00:05:25,446
Two.

131
00:05:25,001 --> 00:05:27,995
Why is the round trip work
of friction never zero?

132
00:05:28,895 --> 00:05:29,795
Three.

133
00:05:29,420 --> 00:05:33,553
Why does gravity do the same work on
the steep path and the winding road?

134
00:05:34,653 --> 00:05:38,118
Next time: a swing slows,
stops and comes back.

135
00:05:38,118 --> 00:05:39,933
Where does its speed go?

136
00:05:39,933 --> 00:05:43,013
Find out in conservation
of mechanical energy.
